---
title: "rate_limiter (Current Finance: Outflow Limiter)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_calc_index: timestamp_index = now / segment_duration
    q_calc_index --> q_mod: curr_index = timestamp_index mod segment_count

    q_mod --> q_add_path: add_outflow(now, value)
    q_add_path --> q_count: curr_outflow = count_current_outflow(now)
    q_count --> q_iter_segments: for each segment in outflow_segments
    q_iter_segments --> q_check_stale: segment.index fresh within cycle?
    q_check_stale --> q_sum: curr_outflow += segment.value
    q_check_stale --> q_skip: skip stale segment
    q_sum --> q_iter_segments
    q_skip --> q_iter_segments
    q_iter_segments --> q_check_limit: assert curr_outflow + value lte outflow_limit
    q_check_limit --> q_update_segment: update segment (reset if new index)
    q_update_segment --> q_add_value: segment.value += value
    q_add_value --> [*]

    q_mod --> q_reduce_path: reduce_outflow(now, value)
    q_reduce_path --> q_reduce_segment: segment.value = max(0, value - reduced)
    q_reduce_segment --> [*]

    note right of q_check_limit
        INV-001: Total outflow within cycle must not exceed outflow_limit
        INV-002: Segments auto-reset when timestamp rolls past their index
        INV-003: reduce_outflow uses saturating subtraction (no underflow)
        INV-004: max_segments = 48, cycle/segment must divide evenly
        INV-005: Limiter is per-asset per-emode (deposit + borrow separate)
    end note
